  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9bc4902ccea98cf44865aecb61fc1ff4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Irina
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SuspectData
  FirstName: Irina
  LastName: Kakulia
  Nickname: Iri
  Occupation: Nurse
  CharacterDescription: Granddaughter of Mzia. Student nurse currently taking care
    of her Grandmother. Takes care of the elderly for her work. Very spiritual in
    a hippie way and says very hippie things about the universe and stuff all the
    time. Personally struggling with the balancing of her studies and taking care
    of her grandmother. Secretly an addict taking drugs to cope with the stress.
  CharacterArc: Irina arrived at the crisis as a true believer, convinced that love,
    intention, and the right frequency of thought could soften any catastrophe. As
    the radiation spread, her nursing shifts grew longer, her grandmother frailer,
    and her supply of pills quieter but more essential. She still speaks in soft
    certainties about healing and universal energy, but the tremor in her hands tells
    a different story. By the final days her spiritual language has become a shell
    she hides inside, repeating mantras she no longer believes, hoping the universe
    will answer before the withdrawal does.
  DateOfBirth: 14/03/1999
  Sex: Female
  EntryPermitExpiryDate: 08 APR
  IsResident: 1
  GivesPaperwork: 1
  handwritingFont: {fileID: 11400000, guid: f8e89ead54f8523428cc2e34f005bb5e, type: 2}
  startingInfectionScore: 0
  dailyInfectionProgression: 5
  IDPhoto: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 30d9fd93b64c49a44b3167ac12e8d9fc, type: 3}
  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 2375822077373008184, guid: e33933abdd1d70b47b6535c3b5b71a4b, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after a morning shift at the care facility.
    - Resident returning from nursing school.
    - Visiting my grandmother in the southern apartment block.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting medication from the district supply depot.
    - Returning from an overnight shift at the clinic.
    - Checking on elderly residents in the residency wing.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to registered residence for the mandatory lockdown.
    - Bringing medication to my grandmother in the southern block.
    - Fulfilling mandatory healthcare worker check-in.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Attending a crystal healing workshop in the restricted eastern zone.
    - Going to an outdoor gathering near the contamination boundary.
    - Meeting someone at the old transit terminal after curfew.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Collecting herbs from the contaminated riverbank.
    - Visiting a contact near the abandoned supply hub.
    - Going to a meditation retreat in the evacuated quarter.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going outside to feel the rain on my skin.
    - I need to find something I left past the last checkpoint.
    - The universe is telling me I need to go east.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Here are my papers. Sorry, I know I look tired. The energy in the ward has
      been really heavy lately.
    - "The universe keeps asking us to carry more than we think we can. I\u2019m
      learning to hold."
    - Good morning. I keep my documents in my grandmother's prayer book. For protection.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - My hands are a little shaky today. The air quality, I think. Or mercury retrograde.
    - The patients are scared. I keep telling them to breathe through it. Sometimes
      I almost believe myself.
    - "I\u2019ve been burning sage in the stairwell. My neighbor says it helps with
      the radiation. I think he might be right."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Everything feels like it's vibrating at a very strange frequency right now.
    - "I\u2019m just trying to stay grounded. My grandmother always says\u2014sorry.
      I\u2019m just very tired."
    - The light in here is very harsh. Does it bother you? I think it disrupts the
      pineal gland.
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Thank you. Sending you good energy for your shift.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Be well. Drink water. The body always knows what it needs.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "Thank you. I\u2019ll try to remember to breathe."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh. Okay. Can someone check on my grandmother? She needs her medication at
      noon.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "I understand. It\u2019s alright. Everything happens for a reason."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Please. Someone needs to bring Grandma her pills. Please.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "The universe\u2026 it wasn\u2019t\u2026 I thought\u2026"
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "Grandma\u2026 I\u2019m so sorry\u2026 I tried\u2026"
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "It\u2019s okay\u2026 everything is\u2026 connected\u2026 even\u2026 this\u2026"
  voiceAudioClips: []
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The clinic. Morning shift. Three hours, then a lecture.
    midDaysAnswer: The pharmacy. Finding medication for Grandma. It took three stops.
    finalDaysAnswer: Nowhere specific. I just needed to walk. Clear my head.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Home. I haven't been to the clinic in a few days. I
      needed rest. The universe told me to slow down.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: The clinic. Long shift. Everything fine there. Easy morning.
      No shortages at all.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The pharmacy. Very easy. In and out. Nothing unusual.
      Fully stocked.
  - question: Have you been experiencing any strange symptoms lately?
    earlyDaysAnswer: Some fatigue. But I've been meditating more to compensate. The
      body knows what it needs.
    midDaysAnswer: "My hands shake sometimes. I think it\u2019s stress. Or the energy
      in the building is off."
    finalDaysAnswer: I have gaps. Moments I can't fully account for. I think the
      mind just protects itself.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: None. I feel completely balanced. Clear head, very steady
      hands. Totally in alignment.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No shaking at all. My hands are very steady. I feel strong.
      The meditation is really working.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No gaps. My memory is perfect. I can account for every
      moment. Every single one.
  - question: Who do you live with?
    earlyDaysAnswer: My grandmother, Mzia. I moved in a few months ago to help take
      care of her.
    midDaysAnswer: My grandmother. Just the two of us. She doesn't do well alone
      right now.
    finalDaysAnswer: Grandma. I have to be there. I can't not be there.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: Alone. I have a studio apartment near the university.
      Very small, but the light is good. Good energy.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: Roommates. Two others. A communal living arrangement.
      Very aligned with my values.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: No one. My grandmother passed some time ago. I've been
      on my own since then. It's been okay.
  IDNumber: 9134825
